    "turn_text": "Mr. Mayor, if we look back over your career, earlier in your career, you were part of Bill Clinton's new democratic movement in 1992. In the administration, you worked closely with fellow centrists like Bruce Reed. on centrist ideas like welfare reform, balanced budget. When you went to Congress, you helped Nancy Pelosi regain the speakership and regain the House Democratic majority by going into districts that had been taken by Republicans and finding candidates who could capture the center. So I do see you in political and ideological terms as somebody who has been an occupant of the center. And yet, the centrist movement that Bill Clinton stood for, to some extent Hillary Clinton stood for, seems really in eclipse in our politics today.",
